 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "Class 7: income of ordinary activities:\n• 70 sales (701 sales of goods, 702 sales of finished products, 706 services sold), 71 operating subsidies, 72 own production of fixed assets, 73 change in stocks of products, 75 other income, 77 financial income (interest received), 79 reversals.\nClass 8: other (extraordinary, HAO) expenses and income:\n• 81 book value of fixed assets sold, 82 proceeds from the sale of fixed assets, 83 HAO expenses (fines, losses from disasters), 84 HAO income (gifts, compensation), 85 HAO provisions, 86 HAO reversals, 87 workers' share of profit, 88 balancing subsidies, 89 income tax.\nThe difference between income (7, plus HAO income in 8) and expenses (6, plus HAO expenses in 8) gives the net result: a profit if income is greater, a loss if expenses are greater.\nResult = total income − total expenses.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {
   "i": 850000,
   "e": 620000
  },
  "problem": "A shop's total income is {i} FCFA and its total expenses are {e} FCFA. Find the result.",
  "steps": [
   "Result = total income − total expenses.",
   "{i} − {e} = {i - e} FCFA; income is greater, so it is a profit."
  ],
  "answer": "A profit of {i - e} FCFA.",
  "checks": []
 },
